<tmc-service-inc>
<pub id="RM0550J">
<servcat id="06">
<name>Brake</name>
<section id="1002J_S000U" variety="S000U">
<name>Brake Control</name>
<ttl id="1002J_S000U_744TG_T0089" variety="T0089">
<name>ABS with EBD &amp; TRC &amp; VSC &amp; BA System</name>
<para id="RM00000060W029X" category="J" type-id="300V4" name-id="443RU-01" from="200912">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Brake Warning Light Remains On</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM00000060W029X_04" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00007S700001">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C154594J02" width="7.106578999in" height="6.791605969in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000060W029X_05" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___0000I6T00000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<ptxt>If the actuator assembly is replaced, perform the "Yaw Rate &amp; G Sensor 0 Point Acquisition" for the VSC system. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000001A8301MX"/>)</ptxt>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000060W029X_06" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM00000060W029X_06_0024" proc-id="RM0550J___00007S800001">
<testtitle>Preliminary Inspection</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Check that the following brake warning light off conditions are met.</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>The ABS warning light is off.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the ABS warning light remains on, first resolve the ABS warning light remaining on.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>There is sufficient brake fluid in the brake master cylinder reservoir.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>The parking brake is fully released.</ptxt>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0025" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060W029X_06_0025" proc-id="RM0550J___00007S900001">
<testtitle>Inspect Connection Condition of Each Part</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Lightly shake the connectors and wire harnesses of each part up and down and side to side, and inspect the brake warning light illumination status.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Warning light display does not change</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the warning light illumination changes when the actuator assembly connector and wires are vibrated, inspect the terminal contacts for malfunctions.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0026" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0036" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060W029X_06_0026" proc-id="RM0550J___00007SA00001">
<testtitle>Inspect Control System CAN Communication System</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70201</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using the SST (TaSCAN), inspect the DTCs and check that there is no malfunction in the CAN communication system. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000001R4W019X"/>)</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Normal DTC</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0027" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0037" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060W029X_06_0027" proc-id="RM0550J___00007SB00001">
<scantool type="4"/>
<testtitle>Inspect ECU Data Monitor (Parking Brake)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70201</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using the SST (TaSCAN), inspect the data monitor for the parking brake switch. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000602011X"/>)</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<title>ECU Data Monitor</title>
<tgroup cols="4">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.77in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.77in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.77in"/>
<colspec colname="COL4" colwidth="1.77in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Item Name</ptxt>
<ptxt>(Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Item Description</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Specified Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Parking Brake</ptxt>
<ptxt>(PKB)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Indicates parking brake operation</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Parking brake applied ←→ released</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>ON←→OFF</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0028" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0033" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060W029X_06_0028" proc-id="RM0550J___00007SC00001">
<testtitle>Inspect Brake Master Cylinder Reservoir Sub-assembly (Fluid Level Warning Switch)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>With the fluid level sufficient, disconnect the fluid level warning switch connector and check the brake warning light display.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Brake warning light does not go off</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the light goes off, the level warning switch has an internal short.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0029" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0038" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060W029X_06_0029" proc-id="RM0550J___00007SD00001">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (Fluid Level Warning Switch - Combination Meter Assembly)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>With the IG OFF, disconnect the fluid level warning switch and combination meter assembly connectors.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C160260J01" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using the SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance of the wire harness side connectors between the fluid level warning switch and combination meter assembly.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.97in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.13in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.03in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1(+) - 40(SW)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using the SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the wire harness side connector of the combination meter assembly and body ground.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.96in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.14in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.03in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>40 (SW) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>10k Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0030" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0039" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060W029X_06_0030" proc-id="RM0550J___00007SE00001">
<testtitle>Inspect ABS &amp; Traction Actuator Assembly (IG1,GND1)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn the IG OFF and disconnect the brake actuator assembly connector.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C146352J14" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using the SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance and voltage between the wire harness side connector of the brake actuator assembly and body ground.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.10in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.92in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.11in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1 (GND1) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.07in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.94in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.12in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>34 (IG1) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10 to 14V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0031" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0040" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060W029X_06_0031" proc-id="RM0550J___00007SF00001">
<scantool type="8"/>
<testtitle>Perform Active Test (Brake Warning Light)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70201</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using the SST (TaSCAN), perform the Active Test of the brake warning light. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000602011X"/>)</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Comes on ←→ goes off according to operation</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0041" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0032" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060W029X_06_0032">
<testtitle>Go to Meter &amp; Gauge System<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000001L5T00JX"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060W029X_06_0033" proc-id="RM0550J___00007SG00001">
<testtitle>Inspect Parking Brake Switch Assembly</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using the SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the parking brake switch assembly and body ground when the switch is operated.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C211519J02" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.72in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.05in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry morerows="1" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1 (+) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Shaft free</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Shaft pushed in</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10k Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0034" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0042" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060W029X_06_0034" proc-id="RM0550J___00007SH00001">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (Parking Brake Switch Assembly - Main Body ECU)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using the SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance of the wire harness side connectors between the parking brake switch assembly and main body ECU.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C223235J01" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.08in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.05in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1(+) - 22(PKB)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using the SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the wire harness side connector of the main body ECU and body ground.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.08in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.98in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.07in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>22 (PKB) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>10k Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0035" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000060W029X_06_0043" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060W029X_06_0035">
<testtitle>Replace main body ECU</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060W029X_06_0036">
<testtitle>Repair or Replace Wire Harness or Connector</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060W029X_06_0037">
<testtitle>Go to Control System CAN Communication System<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000001R4W019X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060W029X_06_0038">
<testtitle>Replace brake master cylinder reservoir sub-assembly<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000002ZRS000X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060W029X_06_0039">
<testtitle>Repair or Replace Wire Harness or Connector</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060W029X_06_0040">
<testtitle>Repair or Replace Wire Harness or Connector</testtitle>
</testgrp>
